  "notes": "Modified cash basis, so basis=cash. All funds governmental (nutrition program is within Other Governmental Funds); no business-type funds. Basic statement from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements, and Changes in Fund Balances Total Governmental Funds column (p4-5). Loan proceeds greater than 12 months (36,500) recorded as debt_proceeds and included in printed total receipts. Transfers (net) are 94,064 into General and (94,064) out of Other Governmental Funds, net zero in total column, so top-level transfers null. Ending cash is the balance sheet total assets/cash 3,410,412 (p6); the roll-forward statement prints ending fund balance 3,410,413 (fund columns 2,247,692+824,847+337,873 = 3,410,412), a 1 dollar printing difference. Beginning cash = beginning fund balance 2,060,393 (p5). General Fund detail uses the General Fund Components combining schedule Total column (General + Depreciation funds, eliminations applied) rather than the more itemized General Fund budget schedule (p11-14), which excludes the Depreciation Fund and includes transfers; not recorded to avoid double counting. Other fund schedules added: School Nutrition (p16), Qualified Capital Purpose Undertaking (p17), Special Building (p18), Activities (p19). Transfers on those schedules (QCP out 100,000; Activities in 5,936) recorded as other financing, signed; the Activities transfer of 5,936 is also printed as General Fund 8000 Transfers on p14 (due to activity fund). Qualified Capital Purpose schedule prints transfers out as its only disbursement line, so no expenditure total recorded for it; Activities schedule prints no total receipts, so no revenue total recorded. Student transportation 247,772 on p9 is after the (200,000) Depreciation Fund transfer elimination (flagged). General Fund Components p8 revenue lines add to the printed Total receipts 8,010,324 (which includes Loan Proceeds 36,500 but not the Transfers - net 94,064, printed on p9 below Total disbursements, outside_printed_total). Support services - Students split by its p4 fund columns (General 417,035 support services; Other Governmental Funds 368,402 student activities = Activities Fund disbursements p19). Balance sheet (user 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of assets, liabilities and fund balances (p6), Total Governmental Funds column. Attempt 4 (targeted re-check): p4 combined lines split using the fund schedules (p7, p16, p18): 'Interest' into Interest Income 34,527 and Penalties and Interest on Taxes 18,902; 'Other' 3,248 into carline tax 55 / license fees 2,070 / corporate grants 800 / police court fines 75 / nutrition rebates 248; 'County sources' into Fines and Licenses 14,926 (code 2110) and ESU Receipts 7,193; 'State receipts' into Homestead Exemption 92,783 / Property Tax Credit 1,594,705 / Motor Vehicle Pro-Rate 8,464 / remaining state aid 2,528,318 (all parts tie to printed lines). Nutrition 'Daily sales - non-reimbursable programs' recategorized to School Lunch Sales (part of p4 Nutrition sales 77,144). Read pages 1-19 of 19.",
